    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Guttenberg-Information-Technologies-Center/Hourly-Data-Analyst_JR100416": {
      "title": "Hourly Data Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Hourly Data Analyst     Reports To: Distinguished Professor        Position Summary: Seeking a Research Assistant to support the final year of a 3-year grant project focused on developing a training model for university counseling and psychological services professionals working with Jewish students. Work will be directed by the Principal Investigator, Dr.   Julie   Ancis. This is a PAID, remote position of approximately 8-10 hours/week    Main Responsibilities Assist with locating several university sites. Communicate with multiple parties and schedule meetings as necessary. Work on theoretical and empirical manuscripts for publication. Keep up to date with, review and summarize relevant literature. Opportunities for related research initiatives. Locate conference and funding outlets. Assist with required report writing. Keep multiple folders organized. Required Qualifications Strong attention to detail and excellent organizational skills. Responsible and reliable. Excellent written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Graduate student Background in psychology, communications, or a related social/behavioral science. Familiarity with scholarly writing; experience with qualitative and/or quantitative analysis. Compensation: $16/hour Additional Information : Candidates must submit a brief cover letter, a Resume/CV and unofficial transcript. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Hourly Employees            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Hourly            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Guttenberg-Information-Technologies-Center/Post-Doctoral-Research-Associate_JR100550": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Post Doctoral Research Associate     Reports To: Professor        Position Summary: Applications are invited for a short-term postdoctoral position on an NSF-funded project on Improving the Security of Large Language Model-Assisted Coding. The candidate will work in New Jersey Insitute of Technology (NJIT)'s Department of Computer Science (CS), primarily with Prof. Iulian Neamtiu, and potentially with other CS faculty members.The candidate will work on a research project that aims to improve the security of LLM-assisted coding by using program analysis and verification to generate code with security guardrails; specifically, expressing safety&security properties formally, encoding these formal specifications into LLM prompts, and iteratively improving the safety&security properties of the generated code.   Essential Functions: Research in type-and-effect systems, and more generally static&dynamic analyses to check the reliability of LLM-generated software Developing program analysis tools and integrating these tools into LLM-based code generation pipelines Mining repositories of, and analyzing large open-source software, using in-house and external industrial verification tools  Presentation of results via peer-reviewed papers and domestic or international travel to professional meetings to present results Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Ph.D. in Computer Science Experience, demonstrated via publications, in using automated theorem provers to check or prove safety of ML/AI implementations Experience, demonstrated via publications, in using static and dynamic analysis to check or ensure the reliability of LLM-generated code Experience, demonstrated via publications, in using mathematical optimization techniques to check or prove software safety Experience, demonstrated via publications, with writing or optimizing systems-level code, e.g., to improve performance or parallelism Experience, demonstrated via publications, with mining and analyzing large, popular, open-source software repositories at scale Experience, demonstrated via publications, with security analysis and finding vulnerabilities in open source software Preferred Qualifications: Experience with type systems, specifically type-and-effect-systems  Experience with symbolic execution Experience with industrial program analysis tools Special Instructions for Applicant: Applicants should have obtained a PhD in Computer Science by the starting date. The start date of the appointment is flexible, however, earlier dates are preferred.  The appointment is for six months, with a possible renewal for up to one year, based on successful applicant performance and funding availability. The preferred start date is October—December 2026. Benefits are competitive and salary will be commensurate with applicant experience. Candidates will need to submit a curriculum vitae, a list of publications, a brief statement of research interests, and the names of three professional references. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: United Council of Academic @ NJIT (UCAN GSRE)            Range: Post Docs            Compensation:   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .            FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Fenster-Hall/Professor-and-Associate-Dean-of-the-School-of-Applied-Engineering-and-Technology--SAET-_JR100616": {
      "title": "Professor and Associate Dean of the School of Applied Engineering and Technology (SAET)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Professor and Associate Dean of the School of Applied Engineering and Technology (SAET)     Reports To: Acting Dean, Newark College of Engineering        Position Summary: About SAET: Founded in 2018, the School of Applied Engineering and Technology (SAET) is the newest academic unit within NJIT’s Newark College of Engineering (NCE). SAET serves approximately 1,000 students across 13 engineering and engineering technology undergraduate programs, with graduate offerings that include applied and research-based study in engineering, technology, and related fields. All baccalaureate programs are industry-focused, with several accredited by ABET and ATMAE. SAET is home to experiential initiatives using the NJIT Makerspace and workforce development efforts, emphasizing applied, reality-based learning. SAET advances innovative pedagogy, knowledge acquisition, and skill development across applied engineering, engineering technology, and industry-focused education. Learn more about SAET’s mission at: SAET-Mission . Explore SAET’s academic offerings at: SAET-Website .   Position Summary: NJIT invites applications and nominations for the position of Associate Dean of the School of Applied Engineering and Technology (SAET) and Chair of the Engineering Technology Department. This is a Professor-level appointment for a candidate with a strong record of research success, academic leadership, and program development in applied engineering or a closely related field. The Associate Dean will position SAET as a national leader in applied education and guide its continued growth in research, workforce development, and applied graduate education. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated history of working across multidisciplinary, interdisciplinary, or transdisciplinary environments, and a demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with diverse disciplines. The Associate Dean will lead efforts to expand SAET’s graduate programs and articulate a compelling vision for growing SAET’s national reputation in applied education. Essential Functions: We are seeking candidates suitable for the rank of Full Professor with a demonstrated record of outstanding leadership and mentorship. Candidates should have strong knowledge of industry-focused education and engineering technology, along with an applied orientation in scholarship, teaching, and program development. The Associate Dean will be expected to build upon SAET's recognized strengths, recruit outstanding faculty, promote scholarly initiatives, facilitate internal and external research collaborations, maintain and further develop already strong relationships with industry, and oversee curriculum development. The person is expected to work effectively in a collaborative, interdisciplinary environment both within the school and college, and across the broader campus to: Provide strategic leadership to advance SAET’s academic and research missions. Position SAET as national leader in applied education, including engineering technology and industry-focused academic innovation. Strengthen partnerships with industry, government, and educational institutions. Expand SAET’s graduate programs in applied, multidisciplinary, interdisciplinary , and transdisciplinary areas, including engineering education. Raise SAET’s visibility in national forums in applied education, engineering technology, and related emerging fields. Facilitate a research environment in the school with active collaborations with academia, industry, and government agencies. Foster excellence in teaching, curriculum development, and scholarly activity. Lead accreditation efforts and ensure continuous program recognition and improvement. Promote and support continued professional growth of faculty and staff and oversee recruitment of outstanding faculty and retention of faculty, staff, and students. Represent SAET to the university administration, other university units, industry, and to public and private agencies at the local, regional, national, and international levels. Potential Research Focus Areas: Candidates should demonstrate research potential in a substantial subset of National Science Foundation (NSF) aligned applied research areas. This can include: Engineering Education and Workforce Development : including use‑inspired research on technology‑enhanced learning, assessment analytics, experiential learning models, and STEM workforce preparation aligned with the Division of Engineering Education and Centers (EEC). Digital Engineering, Digital Twins, and Model‑Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) : including physics‑based simulation, intelligent design tools, and lifecycle digitalization, aligned with NSF’s emphasis on transformative engineering approaches, advanced manufacturing, and integration of intelligent systems. Sustainable, Resilient, and Climate‑Responsive Engineering Systems : including environmental engineering, sustainable energy systems, infrastructure resilience, and circular manufacturing, aligned with Division of Chemical, Bioengineering, Environmental, and Transport Systems (CBET) environmental sustainability programs and CMMI’s infrastructure and resiliency initiatives. Applied Health, Bioengineering, and Human‑Centered Technologies : covering medical devices, assistive and rehabilitative systems, bioindustrial and biomedical engineering, and human factors, consistent with CBET’s bioengineering and engineering healthcare priorities. Advanced Robotics, Controls, and Cyber‑Physical Systems : spanning autonomous systems, intelligent control, human–robot interaction, and networked Cyber‑Physical Systems  (CPS), consistent with priorities in the Division of Electrical, Communications and Cyber Systems (ECCS) and Division of Civil, Mechanical and Manufacturing Innovation (CMMI) robotics and controls portfolio.   Prerequisite Qualifications: Candidates should be able to demonstrate: Record of scholarly achievement and leadership sufficient for appointment as a tenured Full Professor. This qualification normally requires a Ph.D. degree from a recognized institution and a body of scholarly work in a field within STEM, preferably an engineering discipline. Demonstrated expertise and track record in applied education, engineering technology, industry-focused education, or a related field. Demonstrated history of working in multidisciplinary, interdisciplinary, or transdisciplinary settings, with the ability to communicate effectively across diverse disciplines. Proven ability to secure external funding for academic projects, and lead teams of researchers in their successful implementation. Significant experience and commitment for teaching, which include: -Familiarity with curriculum innovation and technology-enhanced learning environments. -Experience with ABET accreditation, program accreditation and course-level assessment. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills, including the ability to engage effectively with faculty and stakeholders across diverse disciplines. Ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, students, and administrators. Preferred Qualifications: Industry experience, either as a practitioner, collaborator, or consultant. Professional license is preferred but not required. Experience with experiential learning programs and workforce development. Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested candidates should submit: Cover letter expressing interest in the position and highlighting key qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Statement of research and teaching philosophy. Contact information of three references. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: PSA Faculty Professor            Compensation: $120,000.00 - $1,000,000.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Tiernan-Hall/University-Lecturer-in-Physics_JR100603": {
      "title": "University Lecturer in Physics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: University Lecturer in Physics     Reports To: Chair        Position Summary: The Department of Physics at New Jersey Institute of Technology (NJIT) invites applications for a 10-month, full-time, non-tenure-track University Lecturer position beginning in Fall 2027, with responsibilities commencing in mid-August 2027. The successful candidate will largely teach introductory undergraduate physics courses, including algebra-based General Physics and calculus-based University Physics I, II, and III. Depending on the candidate’s interests, expertise, and departmental needs, teaching assignments may also include Introduction to Astronomy, Earth in Space, introductory physics laboratories, and/or upper level undergrad or graduate courses. The University Lecturer will work closely with the Director of First-Year Physics and departmental faculty to support coordinated instruction, develop course materials, assess student learning, and strengthen the introductory physics curriculum. The department seeks a candidate committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student engagement, and creating a supportive learning environment for students with varied backgrounds and levels of preparation.   Essential Functions: The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach undergraduate physics courses mostly, but no limited to, freshman- and sophomore-level and, as appropriate, introductory astronomy, space science, physics laboratory courses, and/or upper level courses . Prepare and maintain course syllabi, lecture materials, assignments, classroom activities, and examinations aligned with established course objectives and departmental standards. Work closely with the Director of First-Year Physics to support consistency across course sections, including common course materials, assessments, grading practices, and examination procedures. Proctor examinations, including midterm, final, and common examinations, for assigned course sections and for other coordinated course sections as scheduled by the Department. Evaluate student performance, provide timely and constructive feedback, maintain accurate academic records, and submit grades by established University deadlines. Maintain regularly scheduled office hours to assist students with course content, problem-solving skills, and academic progress. Use effective teaching strategies, including active learning, demonstrations, and appropriate instructional technologies, to promote conceptual understanding and student participation. Use Canvas and other University-supported instructional tools to organize course materials, communicate with students, and support learning. Contribute to course and curriculum development, assessment of student learning outcomes, and ongoing improvements to undergraduate physics instruction. Participate in Department and University service through committees, workgroups, and other activities as assigned. Prerequisite Qualifications: M.S. [Ph.D. preferred] in Physics or a closely related field. Strong knowledge of introductory physics and the ability to teach both algebra-based and calculus-based courses. Strong written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching and student success. Department: Physics Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching college-level physics, particularly introductory lectures or laboratory courses. Evidence of effective teaching, such as teaching evaluations, instructional materials, or other documentation of student engagement and learning. Experience using active-learning approaches and instructional technologies. Experience collaborating with faculty on coordinated courses, common examinations, or curriculum development. Ability to teach introductory astronomy or space science courses. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must submit the following materials: A cover letter describing their interest in the position, relevant teaching experience, and preparation to teach the courses identified above. A current curriculum vitae or resume. A list of three (3) professional references, including each reference’s title, institutional affiliation, telephone number, and email address. Applicants are encouraged to include available evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as teaching evaluations or sample instructional materials. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: PSA Faculty University Lecturer            Compensation: $65,000.00 - $1,000,000.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Student-Mall/Customer-Care-Assistant_JR100637": {
      "title": "Customer Care Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Customer Care Assistant      Reports To: University Registrar        Position Summary: As a core member of the student service team, under the daily supervision of the Assistant Director of Student Support, the Customer Care Assistant assists in the transfer credit evaluation process. Responsibilities include post transfer credits, maintain transfer information within University’s database and website, and credit evaluation work flow. Customer Care Assistant is also expected to serve as the first point of contact for constituents of the Registrar’s Office and to also staff the front desk as needed.   Essential Functions:   Transfer Credit Processing :  Work within the Registrar’s area updating student records across all levels, processing requests from both inside and outside of the office;  Follow-up with students to obtain final transcripts;  Assist with transfer credit evaluation in a timely, accurate and consistent manner;  Maintain credit evaluation workflow and communicate progress with admitted students;  Coordinate document uploads that support tracking the process (approval forms, transcripts, etc.).  Assist at transfer events at other institutions along with the Assistant Registrar Maintain awareness of changes of course transferability Respond to emails and phone calls regarding transfer evaluation  Front Desk/Customer Service :  Serve in the Front Desk and provide information, assistance and referrals to students, alumni, parents, staff members, and the public by responding to telephone, in-person, and e-mail inquiries for the Office of the Registrar.  Access the student database, websites and hard-copy documentation to provide accurate, thorough, and timely responses to telephone, e-mail and in-person inquiries.  Maintain knowledge of NJIT’s policies, procedures, structure, deadlines, and events to provide timely information and appropriate referrals.  Maintain the integrity and security of student and alumni information in electronic and hard copy formats.  Contribute to excellent and appropriately-timed services for all students by collaborating with Student Services and other university staff to facilitate seamless student experiences.  Assist with office processing. Processing :  Work within the registrar’s area updating student records across all levels, processing requests from inside and outside offices;  Access, retrieve, and update student records in databases such as Banner and other digital document management systems;  Post data to the appropriate system of record storage;  Assist in processing data cleanup;  Scan and file documentation  Process cross-registration with Rutgers –Newark, Essex CC, and RBHS. Additional Functions : Provide support for all student record functions in Banner.  Provide processing support to the Registrar and other Professional/Administrative staff members to complete tasks needed to enable the office meet its objectives during peak workload periods, staff absences, and meeting deadlines.  Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Assistant Director of Student Support or senior staff. Pre-requisite Qualifications : High School Diploma Minimum of 2 years of higher education student services experince Functional or operational experience using student information system(s). Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Department : University Registrar Preferred Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution or an equivalent combination of education and experience Experience at a four-year public urban university with an ethnically diverse student body. Direct experience with the Ellucian Banner Student Information System. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Office & Professional Employee International Union (OPEIU)            Range: OPEIU -13            Compensation: $35,315.00 - $47,972.52   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .            FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
