    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Administrative-Center/Talent---Employer-Partnerships-Specialist_JR100620": {
      "title": "Talent & Employer Partnerships Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Talent & Employer Partnerships Specialist     Reports To: Associate Provost, Continued Learning        Position Summary: The Learning and Development Initiative (LDI), the professional education and workforce development division of New Jersey Institute of Technology (NJIT), seeks a dedicated, results-oriented professional for an 18-month, full-time Talent Solutions & Employer Partnerships Specialist role. The position focuses on directly connecting workforce development program participants with regional employers, expanding apprenticeship models, securing work-based learning opportunities, and driving employment outcomes for non-traditional candidates.   Essential Functions: Work directly with LDI workforce development program participants to achieve job placement (providing resume review, interview coaching, job application support, and career guidance). Build and cultivate strategic relationships with regional employers by effectively communicating LDI program graduates' capabilities and career readiness. Explore and establish registered apprenticeship models and work-based learning opportunities, including short-term paid projects, with corporate and community partners. Highlight and advocate full-time employment opportunities specifically for Skilled Through Alternate Routes (STARs) candidates. Drive partner engagement to achieve key program deliverables, including securing at least 10 employer partners who commit to multi-graduate hiring, hosting apprentices, or offering short-term work-based learning projects. Achieve a minimum 60% graduate job placement rate across program participant cohorts. Ensure a minimum 40% 90-day employment retention rate. Additional Functions: Maintain detailed documentation and tracking records for compliance, reporting, and program evaluation purposes. Administer participant career services tracking and course/project materials through Learning Management Systems (LMS) and university databases. On behalf of the program participants, coordinate regularly with workforce development leadership and participate in program alignment meetings as required. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: High school diploma and evidence of post-secondary studies or Bachelor's degree in business management, human resources, communications, career counseling, or a related field. Minimum of 3 to 5 years of experience in a comparable position, such as talent acquisition, employer relations, career coaching, or workforce development. Demonstrated experience establishing strategic business or employer partnerships and supporting job placement initiatives. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, Google Drive Suite Products, and LMS/CRM database applications. Strong oral and written communication skills, interpersonal skills, and problem-solving abilities. Department: Office of Continuing Education/Learning and Development Initiative (LDI) Preferred Qualifications: Associate's or Bachelor's/Master's Degree. Minimum of one to two years of experience in higher education, non-credit continuing education, or grant-funded workforce initiatives. Familiarity with Registered Apprenticeship Programs (RAPs), work-based learning models, and supporting Skilled Through Alternate Routes (STARs) candidates. Ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects, work collaboratively in teams, and adapt to changing program needs. Special Instructions for Applicant: Please note, this is a temporary role with an anticipated end date of May 31, 2028. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: Professional Staff -20            Compensation: $64,978.10 - $105,109.54            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Administrative-Center/Leave---Benefits-Specialist_JR100631": {
      "title": "Leave & Benefits Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Leave & Benefits Specialist     Reports To: Director of Benefits        Position Summary: Under the supervision of the Director of Benefits, the candidate will demonstrate detail-oriented and customer-focused skills as the Leave & Benefits Specialist in the Department of Human Resources & Institutional Access. The employee will serve as a primary subject matter expert administering employee leave programs, statutory leave benefits, health and voluntary benefits, and state retirement plans. This role ensures strict compliance with federal and state regulations, including FMLA and NJFLA—while delivering onboarding benefits orientations and compassionate support to NJIT faculty and staff throughout their employment lifecycle.   Essential Functions: FMLA & NJFLA Management: End-to-end administration of Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA), New Jersey Family Leave Act (NJFLA), New Jersey Family Leave Insurance (NJFLI), and NJ Temporary Disability Insurance (TDI). Interactive Process: Coordinate medical leaves, and return-to-work protocols in collaboration with employees, supervisors, and payroll. Tracking & Documentation: Maintain confidential leave tracking systems, issue required eligibility notices and designations within statutory deadlines, and monitor leave duration limits and intermittent usage. Workers' Compensation Liaison: Serve as a point of contact for employee Workers' Compensation claims and restricted duty assignments Health, Retirement & Voluntary Benefits: Assist in answering employee questions about health, dental, prescription, vision, New Jersey Division of Pensions & Benefits (NJDPB) retirement systems, including the Public Employees Retirement System (PERS), Police and Firemen's Retirement System (PFRS), Alternate Benefit Program (ABP), and supplemental 403(b)/457(b) plans, flexible spending accounts (FSA), life insurance, and voluntary benefit plans offered to NJIT staff and faculty. Enrollment Changes: Process life events, open enrollment changes, terminations, and retirement applications accurately in state and university HRIS systems. Benefits Orientation: Design and conduct comprehensive benefits orientation sessions for all newly hired faculty, administrative staff, and union-represented employees. Employee Support: Act as the first point of contact for benefit inquiries, claims assistance, plan details, and retirement counseling with a high standard of customer service. Open Enrollment: Assist in organizing, communicating, and executing annual open enrollment periods and health fairs. Data Management: Input and reconcile leave and benefit data across NJIT’s HRIS platform (e.g., Workday) and state portal systems (MBOS, EPIC). Reconciliations: Perform regular audits of benefit vendor invoices and state retirement reporting to ensure data integrity and accurate payroll deductions. Policy Maintenance: Stay current on evolving federal/state benefit legislation and recommend updates to university leaves and benefits practices. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a closely related field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Experience: 1 to 2 years of dedicated professional experience administering employee benefits and leave programs. Leave Expertise: Demonstrated working knowledge of federal FMLA and New Jersey Family Leave Act (NJFLA) regulations and administration workflows. Technical Skills: Proficiency with HRIS databases (e.g., Workday, Banner) and standard office productivity suites (Microsoft Office, Excel). Preferred Qualifications Prior benefits or HR experience in higher education or a public/unionized organization in New Jersey. Hands-on experience with New Jersey state platforms (MBOS, EPIC). Core Competencies Customer Service: Strong interpersonal skills with the empathy required to support employees going through life events or medical leave. Communication: Ability to communicate complex policy details clearly, both orally and in writing, to diverse audiences. Discretion: Absolute integrity in handling highly sensitive, medical, and confidential employee records in compliance with HIPAA and FERPA. Organization: Superior multitasking skills with sharp attention to detail and ability to meet strict statutory deadlines. Department: Human Resources & Institutional Access Compensation: $55,000 - $65,000 At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Non-Aligned -12            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .     FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Weston-Hall/Assistant---Associate-Professor_JR100576": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Assistant / Associate Professor     Reports To: Chair        Position Summary: The New Jersey School of Architecture (NJSOA) of the J. Robert and Barbara A. Hillier College of Architecture and Design (HCAD) at the New Jersey Institute of Technology (NJIT) invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty member.  We seek an accomplished architect and educator with a strong research agenda that integrates architectural design with emerging technologies, including areas related to building construction and sustainability. The successful candidate will teach design studios, core courses, and electives while developing a research agenda that strengthens the School’s position within an Institute of Technology and R1 research university. Candidates must hold a Master's in Architecture or a Bachelor's in Architecture with a Master's degree in related fields, as well as a professional architectural license and/or a Ph.D. degree in architecture or a related field. Preference will be given to candidates who have teaching experience in studio and core courses, such as building construction and professional practice. Candidates must submit the following: ●      Cover letter that includes a statement describing the applicant's interest and qualifications for the position. ●      Curriculum Vitae ●      Statement describing the applicant's scholarship, research, and/or professional work. ●      Statement describing the applicant's teaching philosophy with examples of student work. ●      List of three academic/professional references. ●      Portfolio of scholarship, research, and/or professional work. ●      Online Application submitted to https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers   Please provide a link in your cover letter to a digital dossier in PDF Format, including all submitted materials.   Applicants are encouraged to apply by December 1, 2026. The position will remain open until filled.   NJSOA is one of the largest architecture schools in the United States. Our college awards degrees in architecture, urban design, interior, industrial, and digital design. HCAD is one of six colleges/schools at NJIT, a public R-1 research university. The NJIT campus is located in Newark, NJ, within the NYC/NJ metro area. NJIT strives to cultivate a diverse and inclusive campus that promotes excellence among faculty, staff, and students. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: PSA Faculty Assistant Professor            Compensation: $85,000.00 - $1,000,000.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
