    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Fenster-Hall/Assistant-Director-for-CIM-Student-Recruitment---Retention_JR100560": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for CIM Student Recruitment & Retention",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Assistant Director for CIM Student Recruitment & Retention     Reports To: Chair        Position Summary: Reporting to the Director of the School of Applied Engineering and Technology (SAET), the Assistant Director for CIM Student Recruitment & Retention is a temporary position for Fiscal Year 2027 funded by the Concrete Industry Management (CIM) National Steering Committee. The Assistant Director is responsible for promoting and recruiting for the CIM program to prospective students, as well as engaging enrolled students to support retention and graduation efforts. Working closely with NJIT University Admissions and leveraging their enrollment systems (e.g., Slate, Banner, Workday), the individual will collaborate directly with the SAET Built Environment Division (SBED) Academic Advisor and the Coordinator of the CIM Program to execute a unified recruitment and retention strategy. This position manages broad territory travel, high school and community college recruitment, college fairs, and industry outreach. The position requires considerable planning, travel, follow-through, and accountability.   Essential Functions: Student Recruitment & Admissions Alignment: Work directly with NJIT University Admissions and utilize admissions systems/software (Slate, Banner, Workday) to learn, implement, and track best practices in student recruitment. Work with SAET leadership to develop, execute, and monitor a recruitment strategy and territory plan to increase CIM enrollment. High School & Community College Outreach: Handle extensive high school visits, college fairs, transfer days, and broad outreach events organized by NJIT Admissions, partnering with the SBED Advisor. Build and maintain recruitment relationships with community colleges. Data Analysis & Leadership Collaboration: Coordinate with the SBED Academic Advisor and SAET Leadership to analyze applicant pool trends, target demographic data, accepted student profiles, and yield rates. Industry & Stakeholder Engagement: Build relationships with industry recruitment professionals from Patron companies. Deliver presentations on the CIM program for university and non-university audiences, including potential collaborators and members of the Patrons group. Program Marketing & Outreach: In consultation with the Office of Strategic Communication, University Admissions, and the SBED Academic Advisor, execute promotional marketing campaigns and brand alignment for the CIM program. Utilize social media and marketing tools to enhance CIM brand recognition among prospective STEM students. Event & Regional Representation: Serve as the primary representative for broad out-of-region travel, external industry events, and national conferences, utilizing content and program metrics provided in coordination with the SBED Advisor and Program Coordinator. Support major campus recruitment events led by the SBED Advisor, including the CIM Career Fair, CIM Milestone Event, and Concrete Experiential Day. Student Retention & Program Support: Work closely with the CIM Program Coordinator, SBED Academic Advisor, and Director of SAET to align recruitment with academic retention strategies. Support student engagement by directing prospective and current students toward active participation in CIM Student Chapters in coordination with the CIM Faculty Advisor. Participate in CIM National Steering Committee Recruiter and Retention meetings. Additional Functions Work with the SBED Advisor to monitor student enrollment and retention trends to ensure consistency and support actionable outreach strategies. Perform other aligned recruitment, marketing, and retention activities at the direction of the Director of SAET. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited university. Strong interpersonal and communication skills to work effectively with diverse constituencies, prospective students, parents, and industry partners. Demonstrated ability to self-motivate, exercise discretion, manage projects, and work independently. Exceptional public speaking skills and ability to present the University positively to individual students and large audiences. Valid driver's license and personal vehicle required to perform job functions (reimbursed per university policy). Availability and willingness to work regular, weekend, and extended hours, along with extensive year-round travel. Proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and ability to quickly adapt to new software systems. At the university's discretion, an equivalent combination of education and experience preparing the candidate for success in the position may be accepted. Experience working with higher education admissions platforms, specifically Slate and Banner. Experience working in a STEM-based public university or engineering technology environment. Demonstrated ability to adapt quickly to new and changing software and data management systems. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: Professional Staff -25            Compensation: $71,938.82 - $134,163.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Guttenberg-Information-Technologies-Center/Administrative-Coordinator_JR100562": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Administrative Coordinator     Reports To: Director of Administration        Position Summary: The Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative, operational, financial, and programmatic support to the Ying Wu College of Computing (YWCC), primarily supporting the Office of the Dean. This position plays a key role in ensuring the efficient operation of the Dean’s Office by coordinating administrative processes, executive scheduling, purchasing and travel activities, meetings, events, communications, and College initiatives. The Administrative Coordinator serves as a primary point of contact for faculty, staff, students, university offices, visitors, and external constituents and is expected to provide exceptional customer service while exercising professionalism, sound judgment, discretion, and confidentiality. The position supports College leadership in the implementation of strategic priorities and ensures that administrative activities are completed accurately, efficiently, and in accordance with university policies and procedures.   Essential Functions: Provide comprehensive administrative, operational, and project coordination support for the YWCC Dean’s Office and College initiatives. Serve as a primary point of contact for faculty, staff, students, visitors, and university offices; respond to inquiries and direct requests to appropriate College or University personnel. Serve as the primary calendar coordinator for the Dean, Associate Deans, and Director of External Relations, as assigned, including scheduling meetings, interviews, internal and external appointments, and College events. Coordinate meetings and administrative activities associated with College projects and strategic initiatives, including scheduling, preparation of materials, maintenance of project documentation, tracking of action items, and follow-up on deadlines. Process and track financial transactions, including purchase requisitions, purchase orders, invoices, payments, travel authorizations, reimbursements, and other financial documentation. Maintain accurate purchasing, travel, invoice, payment, and related financial administrative records and follow up on outstanding transactions as needed. Coordinate administrative and logistical support for meetings, programs, outreach activities, and College events, including room reservations, catering, audiovisual requirements, signage, event supplies, visitor parking, event materials, attendance tracking, and other logistical requirements. Coordinate general Dean’s Office operations, including front-office coverage, telephone and email inquiries, office supplies, visitors, and routine administrative needs. Maintain administrative tracking systems for purchase orders, contracts, invoices, payment status, travel requests, room reservations, event planning activities, and other administrative requests. Develop, maintain, and update an Administrative Procedures Manual documenting Dean’s Office procedures, administrative workflows, step-by-step processes, and reference materials. Assist with the implementation of new administrative procedures and operational improvements and identify opportunities to improve efficiency, consistency, and customer service. Prepare and distribute routine College communications and monthly reminders highlighting upcoming College events, programs, activities, and administrative deadlines. Review and monitor the YWCC College-Wide Calendar to verify that College events and activities are accurately reflected and coordinate updates with event owners as needed. Coordinate administrative and logistical support for recurring College activities, including K–12 outreach programs, biweekly administrative meetings, College-wide initiatives, and Dean’s Office projects. Maintain planning checklists, attendance records, meeting materials, action items, and progress updates for assigned programs, meetings, and initiatives. Demonstrate knowledge of university policies, procedures, and administrative systems to support effective and compliant College operations. Maintain confidentiality of sensitive information and exercise appropriate judgment when handling administrative, financial, personnel, and College matters. Identify and escalate matters requiring review or action by the Director of Administration/Chief of Staff or other College leadership. Complete special projects and perform other duties as assigned. Additional Functions: Support front desk operations and provide high-level customer service to internal and external constituents. Provide administrative support for special College programs, events, and strategic initiatives. Assist with evening and occasional weekend College events and programs, as needed. Coordinate with other YWCC administrative staff to ensure continuity of Dean’s Office operations and administrative coverage. Support the implementation and documentation of new administrative processes, systems, and College initiatives. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Demonstrated administrative or operational support experience in a professional office environment. Strong proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, Google Workspace, and administrative information systems. Excellent organizational, written and verbal communication, customer service, and project coordination skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, schedules, and competing demands in a fast-paced environment. Strong attention to detail and demonstrated ability to maintain accurate administrative and financial records. Ability to exercise sound judgment, professionalism, discretion, and confidentiality. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, senior administrators, university offices, visitors, and external constituents. Ability to work independently, take initiative, follow through on assignments, and appropriately escalate issues requiring leadership attention. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education administration, academic operations, executive support, or a Dean’s Office environment. Experience providing calendar and administrative support to senior-level administrators or executives. Experience with purchasing, procurement, accounts payable, travel reimbursement, and financial administrative processes. Experience coordinating meetings, programs, events, and outreach activities. Experience developing standard operating procedures, administrative manuals, process documentation, or workflow improvements. Experience using Workday or comparable enterprise administrative and financial systems. Demonstrated experience developing and maintaining administrative tracking systems and coordinating multiple projects simultaneously.   At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: Professional Staff -23            Compensation: $65,603.47 - $121,690.36            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Wellness-and-Events-Center/PE-Karate-Instructor_JR100555": {
      "title": "PE Karate Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: PE Karate Instructor     Reports To: PE Specialist I        Position Summary: The College Karate Instructor is responsible for planning and delivering a safe, engaging, and educational introductory karate course for college students. This one-credit, pass/fail course is designed to introduce students to the fundamental techniques, principles, conditioning methods, and traditions of karate while promoting physical fitness, self-discipline, confidence, respect, and personal responsibility. The instructor will provide developmentally appropriate instruction for students with varying levels of physical ability and martial arts experience. Emphasis should be placed on proper technique, safety, participation, skill development, and understanding of karate principles rather than competitive performance. Course Assessment Because the course is offered on a pass/fail basis , assessment should emphasize consistent participation, effort, safe conduct, and demonstrated understanding of foundational course material rather than advanced technical proficiency. Students may be evaluated on: Attendance and active participation Appropriate effort and engagement Demonstration of basic karate techniques and movement Understanding and observance of safety procedures Appropriate martial arts etiquette and respectful conduct Demonstrated improvement during the semester Completion of any required practical skills assessment or introductory kata Compliance with established course expectations Students are not expected to achieve a particular belt rank as a condition of passing the course unless specifically established in the approved course curriculum.   Essential Functions: Plan and conduct regularly scheduled karate classes in accordance with the college's academic calendar and course requirements. Teach fundamental karate techniques, including appropriate stances, movement, blocks, strikes, kicks, combinations, and introductory forms or kata. Introduce students to appropriate martial arts terminology, etiquette, traditions, and principles. Incorporate warm-up, flexibility, mobility, conditioning, balance, coordination, and cool-down activities into class sessions. Demonstrate techniques clearly and provide appropriate individual and group instruction. Emphasize proper technique, control, and safe training practices at all times. Establish and enforce safety procedures for individual, partner, and group activities. Modify activities when appropriate to accommodate differences in student experience, physical ability, and fitness level. Create an inclusive and respectful learning environment appropriate for a college population. Promote principles associated with martial arts training, including discipline, respect, perseverance, self-control, confidence, and personal responsibility. Maintain accurate attendance and participation records. Communicate course expectations, safety requirements, and standards for successful completion at the beginning of the semester. Evaluate students according to the established requirements of a one-credit, pass/fail course. Submit grades and other required academic records in accordance with college policies and deadlines. Monitor the condition and appropriate use of instructional equipment and training areas. Immediately report injuries, safety concerns, or facility issues in accordance with college procedures. Comply with applicable college policies regarding student conduct, nondiscrimination, accessibility, emergency procedures, and instructional responsibilities. Pre-requisite Qualifications: Demonstrated training and experience in karate. Appropriate karate rank or equivalent documented martial arts experience. Ability to safely teach fundamental karate techniques to beginning-level college students. Knowledge of appropriate martial arts training, conditioning, injury-prevention, and safety practices. Effective verbal communication, demonstration, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with students representing a wide range of abilities and previous athletic experience. Current CPR/AED and First Aid certification, or ability to obtain certification within a timeframe established by the college. P referred Qualifications: Black belt or equivalent recognized rank in karate. Previous experience teaching karate or another martial art to adults or college-age students. Previous teaching, coaching, or instructional experience in a college, university, school, recreation, or martial arts setting. Experience developing introductory martial arts curriculum. Current CPR/AED and First Aid certification. Affiliation or certification with a recognized karate or martial arts organization. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: The successful instructor should demonstrate: Strong knowledge of fundamental karate techniques and training principles. Ability to demonstrate techniques safely and effectively. Understanding of appropriate progression for beginning students. Knowledge of physical conditioning, flexibility, balance, coordination, and injury-prevention principles. Ability to supervise partner activities and maintain appropriate control of the instructional environment. Strong classroom management and organizational skills. Ability to communicate expectations clearly and provide constructive feedback. Commitment to creating a respectful, supportive, and inclusive learning environment. Physical Requirements The position requires the ability to demonstrate and instruct physical activities associated with karate, which may include standing for extended periods, walking, bending, kicking, striking, blocking, stretching, and demonstrating martial arts movements. The instructor must also be able to observe students during physical activity and respond appropriately to safety concerns or emergencies. Compensation: $2668 per contact hour  At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Period Activity Grade            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .     FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Stipend            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Main-Campus-Site/Research-Associate_JR100595": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Research Associate     Reports To: Dean CSLA        Position Summary: The research associate will participate in data collection and analysis, as well as training and supervising graduate and undergraduate students, preparing manuscripts, presenting at conferences, and assisting with grant writing. Candidates nearing graduation are encouraged to apply.   Essential Functions: Conduct education research in different aspects of engineering education by performing interview protocol development, survey development, data collection, and analysis. Prepare manuscripts for submission to peer-reviewed journals and present work at conferences. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students and manage project tasks, including but not limited to data management, IRB approval, and data collection at sites. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: A successful candidate for this position requires strong quantitative and qualitative research knowledge and excellent writing skills. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: United Council of Academic @ NJIT (UCAN GSRE)            Range: Research Associates            Compensation: $44,436.00   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .            FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
