    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Cullimore-Hall/Science-Instructor_JR100033-1": {
      "title": "Science Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Science Instructor     Reports To: Dir NJ Gear UP/College Bound        Position Summary: The Program Instructor (Hourly) – Science for Middle and/or High School demonstrates an overall commitment to the policies and procedures of the New Jersey GEAR UP/College Bound program. This position supports students through academic instruction during year-round programming, including the Academic Year (fall and spring) and Summer Sessions (July through mid-August). During the Academic Year, classes are held Monday through Thursday (with occasional Fridays) from 8:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m. and/or 3:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m., with 20 Saturday sessions from 8:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. School-day schedules may be adjusted based on participating schools. Summer Sessions are currently held for up to six weeks, Monday through Thursday from 8:30 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., with occasional Saturday events. Essential Functions: Provide grade-level science instruction that prepares students for success in high school and college while integrating reading and writing skills into the curriculum. Assist students in developing communication, study, time management, and test-taking skills. Help students build confidence in science while strengthening problem-solving and critical-thinking abilities. Support the development of science, mathematics, reading, and language skills in preparation for state-mandated assessments, including PARCC, PSAT, SAT, and ACT (or their successor assessments). Attend all required staff development and training sessions and submit typed lesson plans in a timely manner. Assist in developing and implementing the NJ GEAR UP/College Bound curriculum aligned with the New Jersey Common Core Standards. Create a positive learning environment that encourages student engagement, self-motivation, and academic achievement. Maintain accurate academic records and student files. Assist with the administration, design, and evaluation of standardized diagnostic and placement assessments. Perform other duties as assigned. Prerequisite Qualifications: Certification in the core subject area of Science. Experience working with minority and disadvantaged students is preferred. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be waived where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the university, an equivalent combination of education and experience that specifically prepares the candidate for success in the position. Preferred Qualifications: $40/hour   Essential Functions: Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Compensation: At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Hourly Employees            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Hourly            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Cullimore-Hall/Mathematics-Instructor_JR100034-1": {
      "title": "Mathematics Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Mathematics Instructor     Reports To: Dir NJ Gear UP/College Bound        Position Summary: The Program Instructor (Hourly) – Mathematics for Middle and/or High School demonstrates an overall commitment to the policies and procedures of the New Jersey GEAR UP/College Bound program. This position supports students through academic instruction during year-round programming, including the Academic Year (fall and spring) and Summer Sessions (July through mid-August). This requisition represents four to six instructor positions, depending on program needs and available hours. During the Academic Year, classes are held Monday through Thursday (with occasional Fridays) from 8:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m. and/or 3:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m., with 20 Saturday sessions from 8:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. School-day schedules may be adjusted based on participating schools. Summer Sessions are currently held for up to six weeks, Monday through Thursday from 8:30 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., with occasional Saturday events. Essential Functions: Provide grade-level mathematics instruction that prepares students for success in high school and college. Integrate reading and writing skills into mathematics instruction. Assist students in developing communication, study, time management, and test-taking skills. Help students build confidence in mathematics while strengthening problem-solving and critical-thinking abilities. Prepare students for state-mandated assessments, including PARCC, PSAT, SAT, and ACT (or their successor assessments), through the development of mathematical skills. Attend all required staff development and training sessions. Submit typed lesson plans in a timely manner. Assist in developing and implementing the New Jersey GEAR UP/College Bound curriculum aligned with the New Jersey Common Core Standards. Create a positive learning environment that encourages student engagement, self-motivation, and academic achievement. Maintain accurate academic records and student files. Assist with the administration, design, and evaluation of standardized diagnostic and placement assessments. Perform other duties as assigned. Prerequisite Qualifications: Certification in the core subject area of Mathematics. Experience working with minority and disadvantaged students is preferred. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be waived where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the university, an equivalent combination of education and experience that specifically prepares the candidate for success in the position. Compensation: $40/hour   Essential Functions: Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Compensation: At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Hourly Employees            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Hourly            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Cullimore-Hall/Mentor_JR100036-1": {
      "title": "Mentor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Mentor     Reports To: Dir NJ Gear UP/College Bound        Position Summary: The Mentor demonstrates an overall commitment to the policies and procedures of the New Jersey GEAR UP/College Bound program. Employment and continued employment are contingent upon successfully passing the State-mandated criminal background check. Mentors serve as positive role models by sharing their knowledge, skills, and experiences to foster the academic and personal growth of New Jersey GEAR UP (Gaining Early Awareness and Readiness for Undergraduate Programs)/College Bound participants. Mentors work with program participants through one-on-one mentoring, group mentoring, tutoring, workshops, classes, and field trips to encourage academic achievement, college readiness, and personal development. The program operates year-round during the Academic Year (fall and spring) and Summer Sessions (July through mid-August). During the Academic Year, activities are held Monday through Thursday (with occasional Fridays) from 8:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m. and/or 3:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m., with 20 Saturday sessions from 8:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. School-day schedules may be adjusted based on participating schools. Summer Sessions are currently held for up to six weeks, Monday through Thursday from 8:30 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., with occasional Saturday events. Additional after-school and during-school hours may be available based on program needs, and work hours may be adjusted as necessary. Essential Functions: Participate in all NJ College Bound Mentor Training sponsored by the New Jersey Office of the Secretary of Higher Education and the Consortium. Provide mentoring support and guidance to encourage participants to pursue and succeed in higher education. Meet regularly with assigned participants in accordance with the established work schedule. Assist mentees in developing the personal, academic, and life skills necessary for success. Help assigned participants establish realistic academic and career goals and expectations. Assist counselors in completing and reviewing each participant's Personal Education Plan (PEP). Accompany mentees on field trips and other program-sponsored activities. Conduct and/or assist with workshops focused on life skills, college readiness, and educational planning. Evaluate and document the progress and experiences of assigned mentees. Provide participants with appropriate academic and community resource information. Commit to serving for a minimum of one full program session (fall, spring, or summer), with exceptions considered as appropriate. Prerequisite Qualifications: Completion of the equivalent coursework of a college sophomore (24 credits) and current enrollment in good academic standing, or graduation from an accredited college or university. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be waived where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the university, an equivalent combination of education and experience that specifically prepares the candidate for success in the position. Compensation: $16-$30/hour   Essential Functions: Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Compensation: At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Hourly Employees            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Hourly            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Cullimore-Hall/Teacher-Assistant-Tutor_JR100035": {
      "title": "Teacher Assistant/Tutor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Teacher Assistant/Tutor     Reports To: Dir NJ Gear UP/College Bound        Position Summary: The Teacher Assistant/Tutor demonstrates an overall commitment to the policies and procedures of the New Jersey GEAR UP/College Bound program. Employment and continued employment are contingent upon successfully passing the State-mandated criminal background check. Teacher Assistants/Tutors are key members of the academic team, working collaboratively with program instructors to provide academic support that helps students succeed and prepares them for college-level expectations. The program operates year-round during the Academic Year (fall and spring) and Summer Sessions (July through mid-August). During the Academic Year, classes are held Monday through Thursday (with occasional Fridays) from 8:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m. and/or 3:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m., with 20 Saturday sessions from 8:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. School-day schedules may be adjusted based on participating schools. Summer Sessions are currently held for up to six weeks, Monday through Thursday from 8:30 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., with occasional Saturday events. Hours may be adjusted as needed. Essential Functions: Assist students in integrating mathematics, reading, and writing skills. Maintain accurate academic records, program statistics related to student resource utilization, and student files. Assist students in developing communication, study, time management, and test-taking skills. Help students build confidence in academic subject areas while strengthening problem-solving and critical-thinking abilities. Support students in developing mathematics, science, reading, and language skills in preparation for state-mandated assessments, including PARCC, PSAT, SAT, ACT, or equivalent examinations. Attend all required staff development and training sessions. Assist in creating a positive learning environment that encourages student engagement, self-motivation, and academic success. Assist with the administration and evaluation of standardized diagnostic and placement assessments. Implement emergency lesson plans in the absence of an instructor. Prerequisite Qualifications: Completion of the equivalent coursework of a college sophomore (24 credits) and current enrollment in good academic standing, or graduation from an accredited college or university. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be waived where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the university, an equivalent combination of education and experience that specifically prepares the candidate for success in the position. Preferred Qualifications: Related work and/or volunteer experience is preferred but not required. Compensation: $16-$30/hour   Essential Functions: Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Compensation: At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Hourly Employees            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Hourly            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
