    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/York-Center/Post-Doctoral-Research-Associate---Powder-based-Pharmaceutical-Product-Development_JR100511": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate - Powder based Pharmaceutical Product Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Post Doctoral Research Associate - Powder based Pharmaceutical Product Development     Reports To: Distinguished Professor        Position Summary: This is a Postdoctoral Research Associate position. We are seeking a self-motivated individual with strong engineering background. The candidate is expected to have excellent hands-on skills, self-initiative, attention to details and ability to engage in experimental research in various projects and be able to integrate available models with the experimental data. Our group specializes in particle engineering and developing model based predictive tools to push the processability of drug products leading to improved quality and performance. The person should also be able to plan and conduct physical experiments. Ideal candidate will collaborate with faculty, doctoral students, and postdocs within Center for Integrated Material Science and Engineering for Pharmaceutical Products (CIMSEPP) which is a NSF Industry-University Cooperative Research Center (IUCRC) at NJIT.   Essential Functions: Lead challenging research topics in powder based drug product development. Projects include enhancing the flowability of needle-shaped APIs and their formulated blends, tackling challenges with the particle scale characterization of spray dried dispersions (SDDs) and developing granular Bond number based bulk property predictions, developing predictive understanding of segregation drivers that adversely impact drug content uniformity, understanding the effect of shear during dissolution of compressed matrix  tablets, prediction of bulk properties of powder blends and process scale up for surface modification based property enhancements and exploring physics-based AI/ML tools to improve predictive formulation development tools. Integrate experimental data with prediction tools including available models and physics-based ML methods.     Additional Functions: Responsibilities include: Leading the assigned projects and developing experimental plans and workflow.   Integrating experimental data, knowledge, and material parameters into modeling framework. Preferably, developing predictive models via a combination of granular physics and AI/ML to predict bulk properties and other key performance parameters.  Supervision of undergraduate and Master’s degree students on their related projects. Be the main point of contact (POC) for all experimental topics and related analytical methods. Disseminate results through peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, and reports to the CIMSEPP Industrial Advisory Board (IAB). Pre-Requisite Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Engineering with significant hands-on experience with particle handling and processing along with modeling tools. Strong expertise in powder characterization, processing, pharmaceutical unit operations, experimental particle technology, and particulate physics. Proficiency in coding for data analysis and applying team-developed predictive models is highly desirable.  At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: United Council of Academic @ NJIT (UCAN GSRE)            Range: Post Docs            Compensation: $63,480.00   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items. To learn more about the comprehensive benefits NJIT offers for this position, please visit our benefits page: https://hr.njit.edu/health-benefits .            FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Eberhardt-Hall/Director-of-Finance--NJIT-Foundation_JR100015-1": {
      "title": "Director of Finance, NJIT Foundation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Director of Finance, NJIT Foundation     Reports To: Associate VP Development & Alumni Relations        Position Summary: The Foundation at New Jersey Institute of Technology is seeking a strategic, mission-driven Director of Finance to lead the financial strategy and operations for a dynamic, student-focused nonprofit organization. As a key member of the Foundation’s leadership team, the Director will be a trusted advisor to the President of the Foundation, Senior Vice President for Finance and Chief Financial Officer of the University, Foundation Board of Directors, and senior staff—ensuring financial integrity, operational excellence, and sustainable growth while aligning resources to advance the Foundation’s mission. \n Essential Functions: Financial Management & Reporting: Lead financial oversight of the annual $1M+ operating budget of the Foundation. Prepare and present financial reports to executive leadership, the board of directors, and external stakeholders. Ensure financial transparency and clarity to support data-driven decision-making. Develop and maintain sophisticated financial models to evaluate strategic initiatives, fundraising campaigns, impacts to the endowment portfolio, and long-term operational sustainability. Develop multi-year financial projections aligned with fundraising and endowment growth strategy to ensure long-term sustainability. Oversee development and maintenance of strong internal controls and adherence to financial reporting practices and all applicable federal and state regulations. Serve as the primary financial liaison between University Finance staff and leadership to understand the financial position of the Foundation as it relates to the University as a whole. External Relations & Fundraising Support: Partner with Development and Advancement teams to evaluate complex gifts, manage donor-advised funds, and communicate financial impact. Lead coordination of the annual audit and preparation of the IRS Form 990, and ensure compliance with all federal, state, and local regulations, GAAP, GASB, IRS, and nonprofit accounting standards. Provide oversight of an endowment and investment portfolio in collaboration with the Investment Committee and OCIO. Develop and maintain a working knowledge of foundations, pooled asset investments, charitable giving opportunities and strategies, and structured noncash donations. Manage third-party vendor relationships and contract negotiations. May supervise staff as assigned. Support executive leadership in evaluating complex gifts and assets. Help craft compelling financial narratives for fundraising and strategic initiatives. Act as a visible ambassador of the Foundation’s mission. Prerequisite Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field. At least 6+ years of progressive financial leadership experience, ideally within a nonprofit, foundation, or similarly complex environment. Demonstrated success in developing financial strategies and managing organizational change. Strong leadership, interpersonal, and communication skills with the ability to engage non-financial stakeholders. Excellent judgment, organization, and communication; ability to manage multiple deadlines and stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications Certified Public Accountant (CPA), Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA), and/or Master’s degree (MBA, MPA, or similar). Familiarity with foundations, donor-advised funds, and philanthropic finance structures. Experience with board members, external auditors, compliance management, and regulatory oversight. Compensation: $105,000-$110,000   At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Non-Aligned -10            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Administrative-Center-Site/Assistant-Director-of-Contract-Administration_JR100141": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Contract Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Assistant Director of Contract Administration     Reports To: Senior Executive Dir of Procurement & Contract Administration        Position Summary: Under the general leadership of the Senior Executive Director of Procurement & Contract Administration, the Assistant Director of Contract Administration is responsible for providing strategic leadership and oversight of the University’s contract administration function. This role leads the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of University-wide contract governance, lifecycle management processes, and stakeholder advisory services. The Assistant Director will oversee all aspects of contract management across the institution, supporting a broad portfolio of agreements including expense-related contracts, revenue-generating agreements, and non-monetary agreements (e.g., MOUs, MOAs, NDAs) across academic, administrative, and programmatic areas. This position serves as the University’s central authority for contract strategy, negotiation, and risk management, working in close collaboration with Procurement Services, the Office of General Counsel, Risk Management, Finance, and other stakeholders. The Assistant Director will ensure contracts are structured to protect the University’s interests while enabling operational effectiveness and supporting institutional initiatives. In addition, the Assistant Director will oversee supplier onboarding as a function aligned with contract administration, ensuring coordination of supplier setup, compliance documentation, and insurance requirements with contractual obligations. This alignment supports efficient contract execution and reflects the integration of contract and supplier processes within the University’s enterprise systems. The role also plays a key role in policy development, process standardization, and organizational change management. The incumbent must be capable of leading a University-wide program, influencing stakeholders at all levels, and managing increasing contract volume and complexity in a dynamic environment.   Essential Functions: Provide strategic leadership for University-wide contract management, including governance, lifecycle processes, and stakeholder engagement Serve as the primary authority and escalation point for complex contractual matters, negotiations, and risk assessment Oversee the intake, review, negotiation, execution, and lifecycle management of all University agreements Lead cross-functional collaboration with Procurement, Legal, Risk Management, Finance, and academic/administrative departments Ensure compliance with University policies, applicable laws, and regulatory requirements Develop and implement contract management strategies that support institutional goals and operational efficiency Drive continuous improvement of contract processes, systems, and tools Contracting & Negotiations Lead negotiation and execution of complex agreements across a wide range of contract types, including expense, revenue-generating, and non-monetary agreements Provide strategic advisory services to University leadership and stakeholders on contract terms, risk allocation, and business implications Evaluate and manage non-standard terms and conditions in coordination with the Office of General Counsel and Risk Management Establish negotiation strategies that balance institutional risk, operational needs, and stakeholder priorities Support departments in structuring agreements that align with University policies and objectives Contract Governance & Program Leadership Develop and maintain a comprehensive contract governance framework for the University Establish and enforce standard contract templates, clause libraries, and policy-aligned practices Lead the evolution of contract lifecycle management processes across all agreement types Oversee integration of contract management within enterprise systems, including Workday Strategic Sourcing Monitor trends, risks, and regulatory changes impacting contract management and adjust practices accordingly Supplier Onboarding and Compliance Provide oversight of the supplier onboarding function, ensuring alignment with contract management processes and requirements Ensure supplier onboarding activities (e.g., tax documentation, compliance certifications, insurance review) are coordinated with contract execution Collaborate with Procurement Services, Accounts Payable, Risk Management, and other stakeholders to streamline onboarding workflows Establish standards and processes to improve efficiency, reduce delays, and ensure compliance across supplier onboarding activities Support integration of supplier onboarding and contract management within enterprise systems (e.g., Workday Strategic Sourcing) Standardization, Systems & Process Improvement Drive the development and implementation of standardized contract processes, tools, and workflows Lead system optimization and alignment of contract management processes within enterprise platforms Develop training, guidance materials, and communication strategies to support campus-wide adoption Use analytics and data-driven insights to improve contract cycle times, efficiency, and compliance Implement change management initiatives to support evolving contract management practices Stakeholder Engagement & Advisory Provide guidance on contract strategy, risk mitigation, and compliance considerations Build strong relationships with academic and administrative units to support contract needs Facilitate collaboration across departments to ensure efficient contract execution Educate stakeholders on contract policies, processes, and best practices Data, Reporting & Performance Management Develop and manage metrics, dashboards, and reporting tools to track contract activity and performance Monitor contract volume, cycle times, and risk trends to inform decision-making Provide reporting and insights to leadership to support strategic planning and operational improvements Establish KPIs to measure effectiveness of contract management processes and governance Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in Business, Supply Chain, Law, Public Administration, or related field 7+ years of experience in contract management, procurement, or related field, including progressively responsible leadership experience Demonstrated experience negotiating and managing complex agreements across diverse contract types Strong knowledge of contract law principles, risk management, and compliance frameworks Experience leading cross-functional initiatives and working with all levels of leadership Proven ability to manage high-volume, complex contract environments Experience with Workday Strategic Sourcing, contract lifecycle management system and enterprise platforms Excellent organizational, analytical, and documentation skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel, Word, and PowerPoint. Ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines. Compensation: $120,000 - $140,000   At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Non-Aligned -10            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Fenster-Hall/University-Lecturer_JR100499": {
      "title": "University Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: University Lecturer     Department: School of Applied Engineering & Technology      Reports To: Chair        Position Summary: The School of Applied Engineering and Technology (SAET) of the Newark College of Engineering at NJIT is searching for a University Lecturer for its Concrete Industry Management (CIM) program in the Built Environment Division (SBED). The candidate will teach primarily undergraduate courses in CIM, and may include both lower and upper level as well as lab courses. The ideal candidate will have a broad set of built environment skills including project management, estimating, and scheduling. In addition, the preferred candidate would have a professional background in concrete: mixture design, processing, applications, repair, delivery, and construction methods. The individual should be willing to work with colleagues to develop new teaching approaches, curriculum, and experiential opportunities in the NJIT Makerspace.  S/he will teach in accordance with the policies and standards of the department and the direction of the Chairperson.  In addition, although this is primarily a teaching position, the candidate may also be involved in other activities in accordance with the terms of the current collective bargaining agreement.   Essential Functions: Maintain regularly scheduled office hours to advise and assist students. Participate in course, program, and experiential learning development as required along with the formal assessment of student performance. Participate in student events and external outreach activities as required. Participate in program accreditation activities. Participate in constituent meetings with the Industrial Advisory Board (IAB).  ​ Initiative: Independently takes action to influence events. Offers own ideas for improvement to promote the goals of the course and curriculum. Seeks feedback from appropriate persons on effects of actions. Identifies a problem, obstacle or opportunity and takes action, including collaborating with colleagues, to address current or future problems or opportunities, within the scope of position as authorized.  Innovative Thinking: An effort to improve performance by doing new things. It can include the introduction of an innovative procedure not currently used, but known elsewhere. It can also include the development of techniques and methods, the ability to go beyond the conventional, and a willingness to try out different solutions. At the higher levels, it is the ability to champion innovation and encourage new ideas from colleagues and students. Flexibility/Adaptability: Recognizes that the environment in which one functions may be constantly changing and adjusts his/her own approach and behavior accordingly. Adapts to and works effectively within a variety of situation and with various individuals and/or groups. This includes understanding and appreciating diverse and opposing perspectives on an issue, adapting one’s approach to the change at hand, and easily accepting and making such changes, whether in one's own duties or in the university's strategic direction.  Leadership: Develops and uses effective strategies and interpersonal styles to influence and guide others toward the accomplishment of identified objectives and goals.  Striving to Excellence: Encourages in students the desire to achieve excellence, both in technical and professional areas. Pursue teaching with technical rigor and professional enthusiasm.  Teaching Pedagogy/Tools : Recognizes different learning styles of students and designs lecturers accordingly to help students with diverse styles, integrates various computation/modeling tools and software as appropriate, and incorporate active-learning strategies and project-based learning. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Candidates with a minimum of a M.S. in Engineering or related field together with strong industrial experience will be seriously considered. A minimum of two years teaching experience in higher education. Preferred Qualifications: Strong preference will be given to applicants with industrial experience, Professional Engineering licensure, and a Ph.D. in Engineering or related field. Special Instructions to Applicants: Rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applications must include a curriculum vitae, cover letter, teaching statement, and list of three (3) professional references. Questions may be directed to the department chairperson, Dr. Samuel Lieber at samuel.lieber@njit.edu. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: PSA Faculty University Lecturer            Compensation: $65,000.00 - $1,000,000.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Guttenberg-Information-Technologies-Center/Director-of-Labs--Education_JR100500": {
      "title": "Director of Labs- Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Director of Labs- Education     Department: Civil & Environmental Engineering      Reports To: Chair        Position Summary: Promotes the educational laboratories in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering, including the laboratories supporting the undergraduate Civil Engineering and Environmental Engineering programs. Instructs faculty, staff, and students in the operation of laboratory equipment used for education. Sets up laboratory spaces and experiments, and calibrates and maintains the analytical equipment used in civil and environmental engineering instruction. Monitors safety in the laboratories. Develops and conducts training sessions, including civil and environmental engineering software applications, for educational programs.   Essential Functions: The Director of Labs for Education is responsible for the operation, safety, and instructional readiness of the Department's undergraduate teaching laboratories. This includes installing, calibrating, and maintaining analytical and environmental monitoring equipment; setting up laboratory spaces and experiments in coordination with faculty; and instructing faculty, staff, and students in the proper and safe use of laboratory equipment. The position develops procedures, training materials, and software-based instructional sessions for civil and environmental engineering laboratory courses; monitors and enforces laboratory safety procedures, including potential service on the university and/or college Safety Committee; and teaches selected laboratory sections such as Strength of Materials, Hydraulics, Geotechnical Engineering, Construction Materials, Soil/Water/Air Quality, Environmental Systems, and Microbiology for Environmental Engineers. Assists student chapters in the development and execution of competitions and other educational projects. Develops proposals to use the Civil and Environmental Engineering laboratories and equipment for educational purposes. Installs and calibrates new laboratory equipment, including analytical instrumentation used in civil and environmental engineering laboratories. Assists faculty with the design, set-up and execution of laboratory experiments. Develops procedures and instructions for proper use of laboratory equipment. Maintains laboratory equipment, including analytical and environmental monitoring instrumentation, and contacts vendors when repairs are necessary. Recommends to the Department Chair new equipment and upgrades of present equipment. Monitors safety procedures in the laboratories, including safety procedures for experiments in process, may be requested to sit on the university and/or college Safety Committee. Develops student training sessions for civil and environmental engineering software applications. Assists in open houses and outreach events. Additional functions include recommending equipment purchases and upgrades to the Department Chair, coordinating vendor repairs, supporting student chapters and outreach events, overseeing student laboratory workers, collaborating with the CEE Director of Labs for Research, and maintaining a flexible schedule to accommodate departmental programs and activities. Performs other duties as assigned by the chair. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: A Bachelor's Degree in Civil Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or a closely related area, and 5-10 years of experience in experimental design and execution, are required. Candidates must possess the ability to understand experimental requirements and to make recommendations on goal attainment. Computer literacy in major civil and environmental engineering software, along with a thorough understanding of data acquisition and the experimental interface, is required. Experience setting up, calibrating, and maintaining analytical laboratory instrumentation is preferred. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: Professional Staff -26            Compensation: $72,048.00 - $135,072.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Tiernan-Hall/Physics-Adjunct-Instructor-for-Labs_JR100351-1": {
      "title": "Physics Adjunct Instructor for Labs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Physics Adjunct Instructor for Labs     Department: Department of Physics      Reports To: Chair        Position Summary: The Department of Physics seeks qualified adjunct instructors to teach undergraduate physics laboratory courses. Adjunct laboratory instructors are responsible for providing high-quality, hands-on instruction, supervising students in the laboratory environment, reinforcing concepts presented in related physics courses, and maintaining a safe and effective learning environment. Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong knowledge of undergraduate physics, effective laboratory teaching practices, a commitment to student success, and the ability to work collaboratively with departmental faculty, staff, and laboratory personnel.   Essential Functions Teach assigned undergraduate physics laboratory courses in accordance with departmental curriculum, laboratory procedures, learning objectives, and course policies. Prepare for and conduct scheduled laboratory sessions, including reviewing experiments, procedures, equipment, and instructional materials prior to each class. Provide clear instruction and demonstrations regarding laboratory experiments, equipment operation, data collection, analysis, and relevant physics concepts. Supervise students during laboratory activities and provide appropriate guidance and assistance while encouraging independent problem-solving and scientific reasoning. Promote and enforce laboratory safety procedures and ensure that students use laboratory equipment and materials appropriately. Evaluate and grade laboratory reports, assignments, quizzes, practical exercises, and other assessments as required by the course. Provide students with timely and constructive feedback regarding their laboratory work and academic progress. Maintain accurate records of attendance, grades, assignments, and student performance. Submit grades and other required course information in accordance with departmental and university deadlines. Utilize the university's learning management system and other instructional technologies as required. Communicate promptly and professionally with students regarding laboratory assignments, course expectations, grades, and other course-related matters. Collaborate with the Director of Undergraduate Physics Laboratories, course coordinators, faculty, teaching assistants, and departmental staff regarding laboratory instruction, scheduling, equipment, assessments, and other instructional requirements. Report damaged, malfunctioning, or missing laboratory equipment and other laboratory concerns promptly to the appropriate departmental personnel. Attend departmental orientations, laboratory training sessions, meetings, and other instructional activities as requested. Adhere to departmental policies, university regulations, laboratory safety requirements, and standards of academic integrity. Promote an inclusive, respectful, and supportive learning environment for students from diverse backgrounds.   Required Qualifications Master's degree in Physics or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated knowledge of undergraduate physics principles and laboratory practices. Ability to safely operate and demonstrate physics laboratory equipment. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to effectively instruct, engage, and support a diverse student population. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, laboratory personnel, teaching assistants, and departmental staff.   Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Physics or a closely related field. Prior college-level teaching experience. Previous experience teaching undergraduate physics laboratory courses. Experience with introductory physics laboratory experiments, instrumentation, data collection, and analysis. Familiarity with learning management systems and other instructional technologies.   Physical Demands Ability to stand and move throughout the laboratory for extended periods. Ability to operate, demonstrate, and assist students with laboratory equipment and instructional technology. Ability to perform routine laboratory activities associated with undergraduate physics experiments. Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and laboratory personnel.   Working Conditions Laboratory courses may be scheduled during daytime and evening hours. Instruction is primarily delivered in person in undergraduate physics laboratories. Laboratory sections generally meet for scheduled two-hour instructional periods. Adjunct instructors are expected to be present for all assigned laboratory sessions and other required instructional responsibilities. The position involves regular interaction with students and the use of physics laboratory equipment, computers, instrumentation, and other instructional materials. Adjunct instructors must comply with all applicable laboratory safety procedures and university policies.   Courses May Include PHYS 102A – General Physics I PHYS 103A – General Physics II PHYS 111A – Physics I PHYS 121A – Physics II PHYS 202A – Introductory Astronomy and Cosmology PHYS 203A – The Earth in Space Other undergraduate physics laboratory courses as assigned.   Compensation $2,668 per contact hour. A typical 1-credit physics laboratory course consists of 2 contact hours, resulting in compensation of $5,336 per laboratory section, subject to university appointment and compensation policies.   The Department of Physics is committed to providing a high-quality educational experience and seeks adjunct laboratory instructors who are dedicated to student success, laboratory safety, academic excellence, and effective undergraduate physics education. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Period Activity Grade            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Stipend            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Central-King-Building/Post-Doctoral-Research-Associate_JR100470-1": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Post Doctoral Research Associate     Department: Biological Sciences      Reports To: Chair        Position Summary: The lab of Dr. Jorge Golowasch invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher to establish a new research line elucidating the bioactivity of plant-derived natural products against neuroinflammation. This position bridges plant natural product chemistry with translational neuroscience, focusing on THC-like compounds identified in liverworts.   Essential Functions: Design and execute bioactivity screens for anti-neuroinflammatory effects in relevant cell models Perform biochemical assays (cytokine profiling, viability assays, signaling pathway analysis) Conduct microscopy imaging (immunofluorescence, live-cell imaging) Integrate electrophysiological readouts (patch-clamp) into the pipeline Maintain and troubleshoot mammalian cell culture (primary neuronal/glial and/or established lines) Handle compound prep, solubility optimization, and dosing for testing Mentor and train graduate students and undergraduate researchers Analyze and present data; contribute to manuscripts and grant applications Maintain records and ensure biosafety/protocol compliance Pre-Requisite Qualifications: PhD in Neuroscience, Cell Biology, Molecular Biology, or a closely related field. Demonstrated hands-on experience with mammalian cell culture systems. Experience with biochemical and molecular assays (e.g., ELISA, Western blotting, qPCR, viability/cytotoxicity assays) Proficiency in microscopy-based imaging techniques (e.g., fluorescence, confocal, or live-cell imaging) and associated image analysis software Strong record of productivity, evidenced by peer-reviewed publications Excellent organizational, analytical, and communication skills Ability to work both independently and collaboratively across multiple research groups At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: United Council of Academic @ NJIT (UCAN GSRE)            Range: Post Docs            Compensation: $63,480.00   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.            FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
