    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Administrative-Center/Chief-Compliance-Officer_JR100004-1": {
      "title": "Chief Compliance Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Chief Compliance Officer     Department: General Counsel & Legal Affairs      Reports To: Senior Vice President of Legal Affairs, General Counsel, and Secretary of the Board        Position Summary: The Chief Compliance Officer (CCO) serves as the senior executive responsible for overseeing and managing compliance with federal, state, and local laws and regulations as well as university policies and procedures. Reporting to the General Counsel, the CCO provides leadership in the development, implementation, and oversight of a comprehensive university-wide compliance program. This position ensures the university maintains a culture of compliance, ethical conduct, and risk awareness while fulfilling its academic and research mission.   Essential Functions: Compliance Program Leadership: Develop, implement, and maintain an effective, risk-based university compliance program. Lead the coordination of compliance efforts across academic, administrative, and research units. Monitor and report on the effectiveness of the compliance program to senior leadership and relevant university committees. Regulatory Oversight & Risk Management: Ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulations (e.g., FERPA, Title IX, Clery Act, HIPAA, NCAA, ADA). Partner with university stakeholders to assess and manage institutional compliance risk. Stay abreast of regulatory changes and update compliance policies, procedures, and training accordingly. Training and Awareness: Develop and deliver regular compliance training and education to faculty, staff, and students. Promote a culture of ethics and compliance across the university community. Investigation and Reporting: Oversee and coordinate internal investigations into reports of non-compliance or misconduct. Maintain a confidential reporting system and ensure reports are addressed appropriately and promptly. Prepare periodic compliance reports for the Board of Trustees and executive leadership. Policy Development and Review: Lead or assist in the creation and revision of university-wide compliance-related policies and procedures. Ensure alignment of policies with best practices and regulatory requirements. Collaboration and Leadership: Serve as chair or member of university compliance-related committees. Act as a liaison with external agencies on compliance matters and audits. Provide expert guidance to university leadership on compliance risks and mitigation strategies. Other duties as assigned. Prerequisite Qualifications: Education: Juris Doctor (JD) or advanced degree in law, compliance, public policy, higher education administration, or a related field required. Experience: Minimum of 8–10 years of progressive experience in legal, compliance, or regulatory roles, preferably within a higher education, healthcare, or public sector setting. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in a university general counsel’s office or comparable environment. Skills and Competencies: Deep knowledge of laws and regulations affecting higher education institutions. Proven ability to lead compliance initiatives in a complex university environment. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills. Strong ethical judgment, discretion, and integrity. Ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with compliance tracking tools and systems. Compensation: $150,000-$180,000 At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Non-Aligned -5            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
