    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/York-Center/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate_JR100427": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate     Department: Dist Professor      Reports To: Distinguished Professor        Position Summary: The New Jersey Institute of Technology (NJIT) invites applications for a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher position to conduct fundamental studies on the ignition of reactive materials. This is a grant-funded position with an initial term of one year, renewable for up to three years total, contingent upon satisfactory performance and continued grant funding. This position is centered on experimental research investigating the processing and synthesis of materials by emulsion-assisted milling (EAM). The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a faculty mentor and closely supervise a Ph.D. student.   Essential Functions: Experimental Design and Execution: Independently design, set up, and execute experiments on material synthesis and processing by EAM. Material and Reaction Analysis: Analyze synthesized materials using techniques such as Electron Microscopy (SEM/TEM) and Thermal Analysis (TGA/DSC). Characterize ignition and combustion of the synthesized materials using different custom techniques, including hot wire ignition, constant volume combustion, laser ignition, and others. Data Processing and Reporting: Perform rigorous data analysis, synthesize results, prepare technical reports for the funding agency, and generate manuscripts for peer-reviewed publication. Mentorship and Collaboration: Work closely with and mentor a Ph.D. student on all aspects of the research project. Presentation: Prepare and deliver professional presentations at national and international conferences Prerequisite Qualifications: A recently awarded Ph.D. in a relevant field, such as Mechanical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Physics, or Chemistry. Demonstrated experience in designing and conducting laboratory experiments. Strong background in electrical, optical, and/or pressure measurement techniques. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a proven record of scholarly publication. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with advanced material characterization techniques, specifically Electron Microscopy (SEM/TEM) and Thermal Analysis (TGA/DSC). Prior experience with high-speed video or other high-temporal resolution imaging techniques. Familiarity with the handling and study of energetic or reactive materials. Experience mentoring or supervising graduate or undergraduate researchers. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: United Council of Academic @ NJIT (UCAN GSRE)            Range: Post Docs            Compensation: $63,480.00   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.            FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
