    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Wellness-and-Events-Center/PE-Yoga-Instructor_JR100399": {
      "title": "PE Yoga Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: PE Yoga Instructor     Department: Physical Education      Reports To: PE Specialist I        Position Summary: The College Physical Education Department is seeking a qualified and enthusiastic Yoga Instructor to teach a one-credit, Pass/Fail undergraduate physical education course. The course meets once per week for 80 minutes and is designed to introduce students to the fundamental principles and practices of yoga in a safe, supportive, and inclusive environment. The instructor will provide students with practical instruction in yoga postures, breathing techniques, flexibility, mobility, balance, relaxation, and basic mindfulness practices. The course should emphasize lifelong wellness, stress management, body awareness, and the development of healthy physical activity habits. Students may enter the course with a wide range of previous yoga and fitness experience; therefore, the instructor should be comfortable teaching beginners and providing appropriate modifications for varying ability and experience levels.   Essential Functions: The Yoga Instructor will: • Plan and teach one 80-minute yoga class per week throughout the academic term. • Provide clear, safe, and appropriate instruction in foundational yoga poses and movement sequences. • Teach basic breathing, relaxation, mindfulness, flexibility, balance, and mobility techniques. • Demonstrate proper body alignment and safe movement mechanics. • Provide appropriate modifications and progressions for students with different experience and ability levels. • Create a welcoming and inclusive learning environment for students of varying fitness backgrounds. • Educate students on the relationship between yoga, physical fitness, stress management, recovery, and overall wellness. • Encourage students to develop greater body awareness and an appreciation for lifelong physical activity. • Begin classes with appropriate preparation/warm-up activities and conclude with suitable cool-down and relaxation activities. • Monitor students during class and provide appropriate feedback regarding technique, safety, and participation. • Maintain accurate attendance and participation records. • Establish and communicate course expectations at the beginning of the semester. • Evaluate students according to the established Pass/Fail requirements for the course. • Submit grades and other required academic documentation according to College and departmental deadlines. • Communicate professionally with students regarding attendance, participation, course expectations, and other course-related matters. • Follow all College policies regarding student safety, accessibility, nondiscrimination, and academic conduct. • Maintain a clean and safe instructional environment and report facility or equipment concerns when necessary. • Perform other course-related responsibilities as assigned by the Physical Education Department. Prerequisite Qualifications: One or more of the following is preferred: • Recognized yoga instructor certification, such as a 200-hour yoga teacher training credential or equivalent. • Previous experience teaching yoga in a college, university, school, fitness, recreation, or wellness setting. • Ability to safely teach introductory yoga to college-age students with varying levels of experience. • Knowledge of proper yoga technique, alignment, modifications, and basic injury-prevention principles. • Strong communication and interpersonal skills. • Ability to create a positive, professional, and inclusive instructional environment. Compensation: $2668 per contact hour At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Period Activity Grade            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Stipend            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Cullimore-Hall/Hourly-Data-Analyst_JR100340": {
      "title": "Hourly Data Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Hourly Data Analyst     Department: Associate Professor      Reports To: Professor        Position Summary: The research assistant will perform research-related tasks under the direction of a faculty member and in collaboration with other team members.   Essential Functions: Conduct interdisciplinary research in mathematical and computational biosciences. Interact with mentors in math and biology to construct mathematical models, perform computational simulations, and analyze experimental data using programming languages such as MATLAB, Python, and R. Prerequisite Qualifications: Familiarity with ordinary differential equations, elementary statistical analysis, and basic computer programming. Compensation: $25/hour At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Hourly Employees            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Hourly            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New 