    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Mechanical-Engineering-Center/Post-Doctoral-Research-Associate_JR100262": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Post Doctoral Research Associate     Department: Assistant Professor      Reports To: Assistant Professor        Position Summary: The New Jersey Institute of Technology (NJIT) invites applications for a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to join an interdisciplinary research team conducting cutting-edge research in flexible and wearable electronics, energy harvesting and storage, multifunctional sensing devices, soft robotics, and intelligent human-centered technologies. The successful candidate will contribute to the design, fabrication, characterization, and integration of next-generation flexible electronic systems for applications in healthcare, robotics, wearable technologies, and human–machine interaction. The position offers opportunities to work on multidisciplinary projects spanning materials, device engineering, robotics, and artificial intelligence. Candidates with demonstrated expertise in one or more of the following areas are strongly encouraged to apply: Flexible and wearable electronics Materials science and engineering Energy harvesting and self-powered systems Sensors and multifunctional sensing technologies Soft robotics and robotic systems Human–machine interaction Machine learning and artificial intelligence Biomedical devices and smart healthcare technologies Printed or stretchable electronics Embedded systems, signal processing, and data analytics The successful candidate is expected to conduct high-impact research, publish in leading peer-reviewed journals, present findings at national and international conferences, mentor graduate and undergraduate students, and contribute to the preparation of research proposals. This is a full-time position with an initial appointment of one year, renewable annually for up to five years, contingent upon satisfactory performance and the availability of continued external research funding. Competitive salary and benefits will be provided in accordance with NJIT policies. Prerequisite Qualifications A recently awarded Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science and Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Robotics, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated research experience in one or more of the following areas: flexible and wearable electronics, soft robotics, advanced functional materials, energy harvesting, multifunctional sensors, human–machine interaction, robotics, machine learning, or artificial intelligence. Evidence of scholarly achievement, including publications in peer-reviewed journals and strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to conduct independent research while collaborating effectively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Preferred Qualifications Hands-on experience in the design, fabrication, characterization, and testing of flexible electronic devices, sensors, robotic systems, or related technologies. Experience with advanced laboratory instrumentation and characterization techniques (e.g., electrical, mechanical, optical, thermal, or materials characterization). Programming and data analysis experience using Python, MATLAB, LabVIEW, C/C++, or related scientific computing tools. Experience mentoring undergraduate or graduate students and contributing to the preparation of research proposals. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary research team involving engineering, materials science, robotics, and artificial intelligence.   - At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: United Council of Academic @ NJIT (UCAN GSRE)            Range: Post Docs            Compensation: $62,232.00   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.            FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
