    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Campus-Center/Marketing---Events-Coordinator--Part-Time_JR100177": {
      "title": "Marketing & Events Coordinator (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Marketing & Events Coordinator (Part-Time)     Department: Student Involvement & Leadership      Reports To: Director of Student Involvement & Leadership        Position Summary: The Marketing and Events Coordinator will support the Office for Student Involvement (OSIL) and Leadership by helping plan and execute OSIL’s Signature events and its comprehensive marketing plan.   Essential Functions: The individual will work with the OSIL team on the following programs and initiatives: Support the planning and execution of OSIL’s Signature Programs Homecoming Involvement Fair  NJIT LEADS Conference  Highlander Awards Greek Week Spring Concert Support the day-to-day operations of OSIL’s student office assistants. Manage processes and procedures related to Recognized Student Organizations’ programs Social Media & Marketing Assist with creating engaging social media content to promote campus events, programs, and involvement opportunities for new and returning students. Capture photos and videos at campus events to highlight student experiences and showcase the vibrant NJIT community. Brainstorm and contribute creative content ideas, including trending social media formats, to increase student engagement and school spirit. Build relationships with student clubs and organizations by helping promote their events, initiatives, and accomplishments through social media. Assist in maintaining a social media content calendar to ensure consistent and timely posts across platforms. Collaborate with the Office for Student Involvement & Leadership team to support marketing campaigns, special events, and campus-wide initiatives. Serve as a positive ambassador for NJIT by creating authentic, student-centered content that encourages campus involvement and fosters Highlander pride. Promotion and Marketing Creating more flyers and designs for university wide events and programs Working with various organizations, departments and offices to help with collaborative marketing tools and resources  Newsletter Create and develop our department’s bi-weekly newsletter. Prerequisite Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required; bachelor's degree or current enrollment in a bachelor's or master's program in Marketing, Communications, Higher Education, Business, Event Management, or a related field preferred. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Strong attention to detail and commitment to providing excellent customer service. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends to support campus events. Familiarity with social media platforms and social media best practices. Preferred Qualifications: Pursuing a Master’s in Higher Education or a related field. Compensation: $20.00 per hour for 15 - 20 hours per week Some weekend work is required. Hours will be adjusted as needed. Start date of August 24, 2026  through May 29, 2027 with the potential to be extended. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Range: Hourly Employees            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.     FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Part time            Pay Rate: Hourly            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Central-Avenue-Building/Coordinator-of-Library-Operations-and-Engagement_JR100196": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Library Operations and Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a current NJIT employee? Apply here through the Internal Jobs Hub.     Title: Coordinator of Library Operations and Engagement     Department: Library Operations      Reports To: Director of Library Operations        Position Summary: The New Jersey Institute of Technology seeks a customer-focused, organized, and collaborative professional to serve as the Coordinator of Library engagement and Operations for the University Libraries. Reporting to the Director of Library Operations, this position supports daily public service operations at the Robert W. Van Houten Library and helps maintain a welcoming, student-centered library environment. The Coordinator supports library events, outreach, student engagement, and communications that promote awareness and use of library spaces, services, and resources. The position coordinates programming, social media, promotional initiatives, and event logistics across the University Libraries. Working collaboratively with library staff and campus partners, the Coordinator exercises independent judgment to support operational priorities and deliver engaging, high-quality programs and services. This is a full-time, 35-hour, on-site work schedule, typically Monday through Friday. Evening and weekend hours will be required based on library operations, events and the academic calendar.   Essential Functions: Service Operations (45%) Works the 9 am to 5 pm shift to support day-to-day service desk operations, provides public service desk coverage, and assists with scheduling for public service staff and student employees to ensure consistent operations and customer service support. Provides patron support for access services, course reserves, resource sharing, account issues, and general inquiries. Troubleshoots basic service issues and refers specialized requests to appropriate staff. Organizes room reservations, event spaces, and service and outreach calendars. Assists with training and onboarding student employees. Maintains service procedures, schedules, and training documentation. Identifies and recommends workflow improvements to support efficient service delivery. Engagement and Outreach (40%) Coordinates event logistics, setup, and breakdown for library-wide events and outreach activities in collaboration with campus partners. Supports operational coordination for library programs and events while maintaining a clear distinction from the instructional and content-focused programming responsibilities of subject liaison librarians. Maintains promotional materials and social media content in collaboration with subject liaison librarians and the leadership team, consistent with institutional brand standards. Assessment and Administrative (15%) Tracks participation and service data and prepares routine reports to support library operations and outreach activities. Maintains outreach calendars, project timelines, and related administrative documentation, as appropriate. Assists with monitoring student employee budgets and operational expenses. Additional Functions Supports day-to-day library operations and serves in place of the Director of Library Operations, as needed, to help maintain continuity of public service and operational functions. Participates in campus committees, meetings, and working groups related to student engagement, outreach, and student success initiatives. Responsibilities may be adjusted as needed to support operational and departmental needs. Pre-Requisite Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum of three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in customer service, libraries, communications, or a related field. Strong organizational, interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Experience using Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and social media platforms used for communication and outreach. Ability to sit or stand for extended periods, or move materials and equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in higher education, student services, or an academic library environment. Experience supporting or organizing student-facing events, programs, or outreach activities. Familiarity with library systems, event scheduling platforms, social media tools, or campus engagement software. Experience working with or supporting student employees in a customer service environment. Special Instructions: Applications must submit the following for consideration: A cover letter describing their qualifications for the position,  A current résumé or curriculum vitae (CV), Contact information for three professional references, including the applicant’s current supervisor. References will be contacted for finalists. ​ Priority review will be given to applications received on or before 09/01/2026 . The position will remain open until filled. NJIT Library recognizes that no candidate is likely to meet every qualification listed in this posting. If your skills, experience, and interests align with this opportunity, we encourage you to apply. At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: Professional Staff -20            Compensation: $64,000.00 - $103,804.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
