    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Campbell-Hall/Program-Service-Coordinator_JR100012-1": {
      "title": "Program Service Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTitle: Program Service Coordinator     Department: NJ Gear UP/College Bound      Reports To: Dir NJ Gear UP/College Bound        Position Summary: Under the leadership of the NJGU/CB Director, the Program Service Coordinator is responsible for the effective implementation of the service components as required by the goals, objectives, and standards associated with the NJ GEAR UP/College Bound grant program at targeted school sites, campus-based and other approved program locations. Essential Functions: Coordinating with the program Site Directors by identifying, recruiting, training, assigning and supervising mentors, tutors, and teacher assistants as needed for program operations in accordance with all policies, regulations, procedures and expectations associated with the grant, NJIT and CPCP. Assisting in increasing program participation by addressing academic and personal needs of students through service component strategies. Supervising the reporting of student services provided by mentors, tutors, and teacher assistants as required by grant, NJIT, and CPCP. This includes the collecting and analyzing of student data from report cards, test scores, Personal Educational Plans (PEPs) completion, etc. to improve service delivery to students and increase student outcomes. Complying with all New Jersey Office of the Secretary of Higher Education (NJOSHE) requirements for Training and Curriculum Development for Mentors. Additional Functions: Perform other duties as assigned Prerequisite Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in education, counseling or a related field with three to five years of experience. Experience with precollege programs and the application of best practices in the delivery of service components strategies and services to increase student interest and success, as well as enrollment in, post-secondary education; Strong management, development, planning, and Organizational skills; and Effective verbal and written communications, computer technology and stakeholder relations skills. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred in STEM and/or K-20 education. Bilingual (written and verbal) in Spanish and English.   At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: Professional Staff -16            Compensation: $63,117.60 - $88,823.64            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Campbell-Hall/Upward-Bound-Counselor_JR100010-1": {
      "title": "Upward Bound Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTitle: Upward Bound Counselor     Department: TRIO Programs      Reports To: Director TRIO Programs        Position Summary: Under the leadership of the Trio Director, the Upward Bound Counselor provides academic, career, and educational counseling, as well as assistance with completing the college admissions and financial aid process. The counselor also provides motivational support and advocates for program participants. Other services the UB Counselor coordinates include academic instruction, mentoring, and tutoring. The Upward Bound Counselor is responsible for effectively implementing and achieving all goals, objectives, and standards associated with the Upward Bound Program as outlined by the US Department of Education. During the academic year, there are 26 to 28 sessions on Saturdays that run from 8:30 am until 2:30 pm. There is also an afterschool program that runs Monday through Thursday from 3:00 pm until 6:00 pm as well as evening orientations and activities that are typically scheduled from 6 pm until 8:00 pm. A six-week summer program is conducted, with up to five of those weeks being residential. During the summer program, staff are expected to be available on campus, for overnight supervision of students for the duration of the residential program and should expect to work longer hours during the day. Saturday and off-hour work is required. Essential Functions: Screen middle (8th graders) and high school students to determine eligibility. Collect, analyze, and maintain student data, including report cards, test scores, and Personal Educational Plans to improve student service delivery and increase student outcomes. Develop and maintain a file on each eligible participant for use in education and career planning. Supervise and conduct group counseling, individual counseling, and personal development activities. Organize and conduct career workshops, seminars, and other educational activities. Conduct entrance and exit interviews of program participants. Assist the program director with program planning and evaluation, reviewing applications for college admission, and financial aid, assessing education needs, and developing goals of project participants. Conduct entrance and exit interviews of program participants. Organize and conduct career workshops, seminars, and other educational activities. Must be willing to make off-site visits to target schools regularly. Additional Functions: Assisting in developing program proposals and preparing reports. Developing and implementing curriculum. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director. Prerequisite Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in counseling, Student Personnel Services, Social Work, Psychology, Education, or related fields. Two or more years of counseling experience, academic advising, or teaching experience at the middle school, high school, or post-secondary level. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated skills in individual and group counseling techniques. Experience in conducting testing and training activities. Basic knowledge of the Microsoft Suite and the Google Suite. Work on Saturdays and during off-hours is required. Must be able to provide overnight supervision on campus for the duration of the residential summer program (overnight duties will be split between appropriate staff). Must be able to provide overnight supervision on campus for the duration of the residential summer program (overnight duties will be split between appropriate staff). Must have a valid driver's license and access to a vehicle. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in counseling, Student Personnel Services,Social Work, Psychology, Education, or a related field. Experience working in STEM and/or K-20 education. Experience working with the underserved and low-income, first-generation student population. Knowledge of TRiO programs is helpful.   At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Professional Staff Association (PSA)            Range: Professional Staff -20            Compensation: $64,000.00 - $103,804.00            NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.   FLSA: Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
    },
    "https://njit.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NJIT_Careers/job/Campbell-Hall/Administrative-Assistant-III_JR100008-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant III",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTitle: Administrative Assistant III     Department: NJ Gear UP/College Bound      Reports To: Dir NJ Gear UP/College Bound        Position Summary: Under the leadership of Director of the Consortium for Pre-College Program Education in Greater Newark/NJ GEAR UP/NJ College Bound, the Program Administrative Assist is responsible for administrative matters related to the efficient and effective operation of the Consortium. This position requires an individual to constantly learn and administer all university policies and procures for processing. Essential Functions: Serves as departmental point of contact; coordinates phone and mail requests for department. Schedules travel and accommodation requirements for department utilizing and adhering to all universities polices through use of Anthony Travel or other university procures and practices as directed. Greets and provides information and assistance to office visitors by providing exceptional service /support in accordance with departmental policies and procedures. Schedules and coordinates all appointments, meetings, etc. that includes accommodations, including initial and follow-up contact as requested by professional staff. Assists with overseeing student office workers and coordinates timekeeping and payroll processing for all part-time staff through university’s Banner system. Creates and maintains filing system for personnel and purchases correspondence and other areas to support efficient and effective program operation. Handles administrative support aspects of standard and special events such as weekday and Saturday campus activities, field trips, college tours, etc. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to reserving rooms (Live25), media equipment (Media Technology Support Services’ online system); processing food orders through university’s Gourmet Dining Services system, working with Facilities division for furniture set ups; and assisting with preparing budget reports. Coordinates and follows up on all requisitions for program and office purchases through NJIT’s Highlander eMerchant system. Assist in preparing all correspondence materials such as emails, flyers, notices, applications, surveys, forms, etc. from drafts to final versions using MS office products and or similar applications for word processing, spreadsheet, and desktop publishing printed and/or online versions. Maintains confidentiality in all areas of program personnel and program matters. Additional Functions: Assists with the orientation, training, and assignment of student employees. Provide minutes from meetings. Perform duties outside of NJIT business hours such as early morning, evening, and/or Saturday program support. Performs other duties as required. Coordinates and serves as liaison with other departmental units in maintaining program and departmental services such as supplies, maintenance, repairs, mail, publicity, community outreach, etc. Prerequisite Qualifications: Minimum of 3 years previous experience in a comparable administrative position. Must be proficient in personal computing using electronic mail, Microsoft Office Suite applications, Google Drive Suite Products, and/or compatible applications or services. Must possess strong oral and written communication and problem solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: Associate’s Degree. One to two years’ experience preferably in a higher education environment.   At the university's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the university an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position.            Union: Office & Professional Employee International Union (OPEIU)            Range: OPEIU -18            Compensation: $43,979.00 - $60,029.33   NJIT considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. This pay range represents base pay only and excludes any additional items such as incentives, bonuses, or other items.            FLSA: Non-Exempt            Time Type: Full time            Pay Rate: Salary            Additional Information: As an EEO employer NJIT is committed to building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment and strongly encourages applications from individuals with disabilities, minorities, veterans, and women. Employment at NJIT is subject to the provisions of New Jersey First Act which mandates new employees, who are not NJ residents, to establish primary residence in New Jersey within one year of their appointment to certain positions. The law does not apply to any individual employed at NJIT on a temporary or per semester basis as a visiting or adjunct professor, teacher, lecturer, researcher or administrator. For more information on the act please click here. If special accommodations are needed in applying for a position, please visit the Department of Human Resources located in Fenster Hall, 5th Floor, University Heights, Newark, NJ 07102 or call (973) 596-3140. If you have questions, please email the Human Resources Department at hr@njit.edu. Information regarding NJIT campus security, personal safety, and fire safety including topics such as, disciplinary procedures, crime prevention, NJIT Police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, and crime statistics for the most recent three year period is available on the NJIT Department of Public Safety here . NJIT is an E-Verify employer and uses E-Verify to confirm work authorization of each new hire."
